              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              (see there) only that where there one may choose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+covers"} good open covers
              here we have to choose genuine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+hypercovers"} split hypercovers
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polydiscs"} polydiscs
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            %p
              To start with, since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
              depends only on the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              of a site we may represent
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Analytic
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi lwhe
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Discs
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{C}Analytic\infty Grpd
                    \\simeq
                    L_{lwhe} sPSh(\mathbb{C}Discs)_{proj, loc}
            %p
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi Disc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}Disc
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} localized
              (by the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "hypercover#DescentFromDescentAlongHypercovers"} theorem of descent recognition along hypercovers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\bullet\to X
              as seen over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CplxMfd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CplxMfd
              restricted to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polydisc"} polydisc
              (this roundabout way since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Disc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}Disc
              does not carry a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              but just a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            %p
              Now before
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
              we have a simplicially enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Disc
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi Δ
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sPSh(\mathbb{C}Disc)_{proj, loc}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\underset{\to}{\lim}}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{\Delta}{\longleftarrow}}
                    sSet_{Quillen}
            %p
              which is simplicial-degree wise just the defining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\to}{\lim}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+presheaf"} constant presheaf
              functor.
            %p
              To see that this descends to a Quillen adjunction on the local model structure, by the
              %a{:href => "Quillen+adjunction#RecognitionOfSimplicialQuillenAdjunctions"} recognition theorem for simplicial Quillen adjunctions
              we hence need to check that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              preserves fibrant objects with respect to the local model structure, hence that any constant simplicial presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta S
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              already satisfies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
              as seen over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CplxMfd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CplxMfd
            %p
              By the
              %a{:href => "hypercover#DescentFromDescentAlongHypercovers"} theorem of descent recognition along hypercovers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta S
              satisfies descent precisely if for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\bullet \to X
              of any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polydisc"} polydisc
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-spaces"} derived hom-spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RHom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi RHom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    RHom(X, \Delta S) \longrightarrow RHom(U_\bullet, \Delta S)
            %p
              in the global
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RHom
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RHom
              in turn may be computed as the
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+object"} hom object
              out of a cofibrant resolution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \to X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo •
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat U_\bullet \to U_\bullet
              %a{:href => "model%20structure%20on%20simplicial%20presheaves#CofibrantObjects"} recognition of cofibrant objects in the projective model structure
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is already cofibrant and a sufficient condition for a resolution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat U_\bullet \to U_\bullet
              to be cofibrant is that it is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+hypercover"} split hypercover
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi CplxMfd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}Disc \hookrightarrow CplxMfd
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subsite"} dense subsite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat U_\bullet
              consists simplicial-degreewise of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polydiscs"} polydiscs
              %em
                %a{:href => "hypercover#ExistenceOfSplitRefinements"} hypercover – Existence of split refinements
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
              is the point, this means that with such a choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\to}{\lim} \hat U_\bullet
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              obtained by replacing in the hypercover by polydiscs each polydisc by a point. Forgetting the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
              on all manifolds involved, one sees that this is precisely the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+homotopy+type"}> etale homotopy type
              ” of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as seen by the site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              of the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+homotopy+type"} contractible
            %p In conclusion this means that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi RHom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi sPSh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℂ
                            %mi Disc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi sSet
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Sing
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi sSet
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    RHom(U_\bullet, \Delta S)
                    \&amp;\simeq
                    sPSh(\mathbb{C}Disc)(\hat U_\bullet, \Delta S)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    sSet(Sing(X), S)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    sSet(\ast, S)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\simeq S
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Therefore the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              condition for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta S
              is satisfied. (This is also the statement of (
              %a{:href => "#HopkinsQuick12"}> Hopkins-Quick 12, lemma 2.3, prop. 2.4, lemma 2.5, prop. 2.6
              )).
            %p
              From here on the argument for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Analytic
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}Analytic \infty Grpd
              proceeds as at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-cohesive+site"} ∞-cohesive site
              (which might just as well be adapted to the hyper-discussion here).
          #ShapeOfComplexManifold.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CplxMfd
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Analytic
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in CplxMfd \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}Analytic\infty Grpd
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              of its underlying
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#HopkinsQuick12"}> Hopkins-Quick 12
            )) this is part of prop. 2.6.
          %h3#OkaPrinciple Oka principle
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oka+principle"} Oka principle
            in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mi Analytic
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}Analytic\infty Grpd
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#Larusson01"}> Larusson 01
            ).
          #OkaManifold.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Say that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is an
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oka+manifold"} Oka manifold
              if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stein+manifold"} Stein manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              the canonical inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Maps
                      %mi hol
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi Maps
                      %mi top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Maps_{hol}(\Sigma, X) \longrightarrow Maps_{top}(\Sigma, X)
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
              to that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              (both equipped with the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              This is the case precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Maps
                      %mi hol
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Psh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SteinSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps_{hol}(-,X) \in Psh_\infty(SteinSp)
              satisfies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covers"} covers
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Larusson01"}> Larusson 01, theorem 2.1
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              By corollary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShapeOfComplexManifold"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Cohesion"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OkaManifold"}
              should (…check…) read
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi[\Sigma,X] \simeq \flat [\Pi(\Sigma), \Pi(X)]
                    \\,.
          %h3#DifferentialCohomology Complex analytic differential generalized cohomology
          %p
            By prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Cohesion"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mi Analytic
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}Analytic \infty Grpd
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive
            and hence by the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+hexagon"} differential cohomology hexagon
            the objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mi Analytic
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E \in Stab(\mathbb{C}Analytic \infty Grpd)
            (hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+spectra"} sheaves of spectra
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mi Mfd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}Mfd
            ) qualify as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            refinements of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theories"} cohomology theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represented
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shapes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Π
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\coloneqq \Pi \hat E \in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
          %p
            Discussion of such complex analytic differential generalized cohomology is in (
            %a{:href => "#HopkinsQuick12"}> Hopkins-Quick 12, section 4
            ),.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#multiplicative_group_and_holomorphic_line_bundles
            Multiplicative group and holomorphic line
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group"} multiplicative group
            is a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mi Analytic
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{G}_m \in Grp(\mathbb{C}Analytic\infty Grpd)
          %p
            given as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaf"} (∞,1)-presheaf
            by the assignment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ↦
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{G}_m \;\colon\; \Sigma \mapsto \mathcal{O}_\Sigma^\times
          %p
            that sends a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stein+manifold"} Stein manifold
            to the multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            of non-vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
            on it.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}_m
            is the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundles"} holomorphic line bundles
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+stack"} Picard stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}_m
            that for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+2-bundles"} holomorphic line 2-bundles
            (the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+stack"} Brauer stack
